    1: # Rendering Architecture
    2: 
    3: Stage 5 splits block rendering behind an extension point so consumers can replace
    4: how a block type paints without forking the editor widget. This document covers
    5: the registry contract, the default renderers, and the virtualisation / dirty
    6: work still on the roadmap.
    7: 
    8: ## Block renderer registry
    9: 
   10: `lib/src/widgets/block_renderer_registry.dart` defines the indirection:
   11: 
   12: - `BlockRendererRegistry` — maps `BlockType` and custom
   13:   `BlockEmbedNode.embedType` → `BlockRendererBuilder`.
   14: - `BlockRendererBuilder` — `Widget Function(BuildContext, BlockRenderContext)`.
   15: - `BlockRenderContext` — bundles everything a renderer needs: the `BlockNode`,
   16:   its `blockIndex`, the active `DocumentSelection`, the IME
   17:   `CompositionState`, the `BlockGeometryRegistry` (for hit-testing), the
   18:   `showCaret` flag, the ambient `textStyle`, the `showDebugOverlay` flag, and
   19:   optional code/callout/table hooks (`onCodeLanguageChanged`, `onCodeCopied`,
   20:   `onCalloutVariantChanged`, `onTableToolbarAction`, `onTableColumnResize`).
   21: 
   22: The editor consults the registry once per block in `_BlockRenderer.build`. When
   23: no builder is registered for a block's type, the editor falls back to a
   24: plain-text `Text(block.plainText)` so an unknown type always paints something.
   25: 
   26: ## Wiring a custom renderer
   27: 
   28: Two equivalent entry points:
   29: 
   30: 1. **Implicit (defaults provided).** Omit `WenzRichTextEditor.blockRenderers`.
   31:    The editor builds a private registry with the built-in defaults installed.
   32:    Use this when you only want default behaviour.
   33: 
   34: 2. **Explicit (override what you need).** Construct a `BlockRendererRegistry`,
   35:    seed it with `WenzRichTextEditor.installDefaultRenderers(registry)`, then
   36:    `register` overrides for block types or `registerEmbed` overrides for
   37:    business embed types. Pass it via `blockRenderers`.
   38: 
   39: ```dart
   40: final registry = BlockRendererRegistry();
   41: WenzRichTextEditor.installDefaultRenderers(registry);
   42: registry.register(BlockType.image, (context, rc) {
   43:   return MyImageDecoder(assetId: (rc.block as ImageBlockNode).assetId);
   44: });
   45: 
   46: WenzRichTextEditor(
   47:   controller: controller,
   48:   blockRenderers: registry,
   49: );
   50: ```
   51: 
   52: A custom renderer receives the same `BlockRenderContext` the built-ins do. For
   53: atomic object blocks, wrap the custom widget in
   54: `WenzObjectBlockSurface(renderContext: rc, child: widget)` to keep selection
   55: highlight, geometry registration, caret anchoring, and debug-overlay behaviour;
   56: or ignore the surface and paint freely.
   57: 
   58: ## Block embed renderer injection
   59: 
   60: `BlockEmbedNode` is the generic block-level embed model for business content
   61: such as CRM cards, link previews, diagrams, or external workflow panels. It
   62: stores `embedType`, JSON-compatible `data`, and `fallbackText`.
   63: 
   64: ```dart
   65: final registry = BlockRendererRegistry();
   66: WenzRichTextEditor.installDefaultRenderers(registry);
   67: registry.registerEmbed('crm-card', (context, rc) {
   68:   final embed = rc.block as BlockEmbedNode;
   69:   return WenzObjectBlockSurface(
   70:     renderContext: rc,
   71:     child: CrmCard(recordId: embed.data['recordId'] as String),
   72:   );
   73: });
   74: 
   75: controller.insertBlockEmbed(
   76:   blockId: 'crm-1',
   77:   embedType: 'crm-card',
   78:   data: <String, Object?>{'recordId': '42'},
   79:   fallbackText: 'Acme account',
   80: );
   81: ```
   82: 
   83: Resolution order for `BlockEmbedNode`: an exact `registerEmbed(embedType, ...)`
   84: builder wins; otherwise the generic `BlockType.embed` renderer paints the built-
   85: in placeholder. Rich JSON and HTML round-trip the structured embed fields;
   86: Markdown/plain text intentionally degrade to readable fallback text.
   87: 
   88: ## Default renderers
   89: 
   90: `WenzRichTextEditor.installDefaultRenderers` registers one builder per
   91: `BlockType`:
   92: 
   93: | BlockType | Renderer | Notes |
   94: | --- | --- | --- |
   95: | paragraph / heading / quote / listItem | `_TextBlockRenderer` | Inline-aware; formula/mention fallback + optional `InlineEmbedRenderer`; selection/caret/composition via `_TextSelectionSurface`. |
   96: | code | `_CodeBlockRenderer` | Monospace body with composition underline span; toolbar includes language dropdown and copy-code button. Language changes call `SetCodeLanguageCommand`; Tab/Shift+Tab in the editor call `IndentCodeBlockCommand`. |
   97: | image / video / file | asks `MediaResolver`, then built-in fallback | Built-in media renderers consult the injected [MediaResolver] first; when it returns `null` (or no resolver is set) images/videos fall back to `_MediaPlaceholder`, while files fall back to a metadata card. Image blocks wrap the result with `showWidth`/`showHeight` sizing and optional caption text; file cards show display name, size, MIME type, upload status, and failure text. See [Media resolver](#media-resolver). |
   98: | embed | `_BlockEmbedContent` or business renderer | Generic block embed placeholder displays `embedType` + `fallbackText`/data label. Register per business type with `BlockRendererRegistry.registerEmbed`; wrap large custom widgets in `WenzObjectBlockSurface` for object-block selection semantics. |
   99: | table | `_TableBlockRenderer` | Custom Stack grid layout; visible cells are positioned by `rowSpan`/`columnSpan`, covered cells are not rendered or hit-tested; table-cell text uses the same inline embed fallback/renderer path. When a table cell/range is selected, the default renderer shows a floating toolbar for row/column insert/delete, header/background/alignment, merge/split, width reset, plus drag handles that persist explicit column widths via `SetTableColumnWidthCommand`. |
  100: | divider | Flutter `Divider`. | |
  101: | callout | `_CalloutRenderer` | Variant-tinted surface with icon, title, body, and an editable type dropdown for `info`/`success`/`warning`/`danger`; uses the same inline embed fallback/renderer path. |
