    4: /// Exports a [RichTextDocument] as plain text.
    5: ///
    6: /// Each block contributes one paragraph (its [BlockNode.plainText]); blocks
    7: /// are separated by a blank line so the output reads as paragraphs rather
    8: /// than a single run-on line. Non-text blocks (divider/image/video/file) that
    9: /// carry no plain text are rendered as a short sentinel so the reader can see
   10: /// where they sat in the flow; pass [omitEmptyBlocks] = true to drop them
   11: /// entirely.
   12: ///
   13: /// This is a one-way export — there is no plain-text *import* (parsing
   14: /// unstructured text back into block structure is the job of the Markdown /
   15: /// HTML codecs, stage 6). Use it for "copy document as text", search
   16: /// indexing, and export-to-`.txt` workflows.
   17: class PlainTextCodec {
   18:   const PlainTextCodec({this.omitEmptyBlocks = false});
   19: 
   20:   /// When true, blocks whose [BlockNode.plainText] is empty are skipped
   21:   /// instead of emitting a sentinel line. Default is `false` so the export
   22:   /// always reflects document structure.
   23:   final bool omitEmptyBlocks;
   24: 
   25:   String encode(RichTextDocument document) {
   26:     final lines = <String>[];
