  129: ## Code block line numbers
  130: 
  131: Code line numbers are a renderer concern, not document content:
  132: 
  133: - They are derived from `CodeBlockNode.code` at paint time and never persist to
  134:   `CodeBlockNode`, rich/legacy JSON, Markdown, HTML, plain-text export,
  135:   clipboard payloads, command history, or undo/redo snapshots.
  136: - Numbering is 1-based. The line count is `code.split('\n').length`, so empty
  137:   code displays line `1`, blank lines are counted, consecutive newlines produce
  138:   blank numbered rows, and a trailing newline produces a final empty numbered
  139:   row.
  140: - The line-number gutter sits to the left of the code text, uses the same
  141:   monospace family, `13.5px` font size, and `1.6` line height as code content,
  142:   aligns labels to the right, uses `0x8AE6E6F0`, and keeps `12px` between the
  143:   gutter and code text.
  144: - The gutter is not part of `_TextSelectionSurface`: it does not participate in
  145:   text offset mapping, selection, caret/composition rectangles, find highlights,
  146:   Tab indentation, language changes, or copy-code output.
  147: - Horizontal scrolling moves only the code text surface; the line-number gutter
  148:   remains visually anchored at the left edge of the code block so long lines can
  149:   scroll without dragging line numbers away from their rows.
  150: 
  151: ## Media resolver
  152: 
  153: `MediaResolver` (`lib/src/widgets/media_resolver.dart`) is the quick path for
